# Removed Obsolete Paths (Cumulative)

22 dead-code items; prompts/list; sampling; roots/list; notifications/roots/list_changed; dynamic graph state; per-instance dynamic graph; request-reply only; mcp_graph_to_json on every read; boards as single block; 8 redteam gates; graph capabilities; single-instance graph; static codex; cache survives lineage; redteam graph dirty; cache.sha vs disk; lineage log writable; G16 fires only at close; G15 quarantine dirty; fs peer exchange; caps outlive codex; hard-coded 10-epoch; G17D snapshot only; silent cap demotion; 5-bit cap bitmask; single-host gossip; unbounded lineage; best-effort immediate emit; mcp_g18_cap_revocation.oo revalidate; queue drained at close; single-shot TCP; manual compaction; never called by server; exposed not auto-wired; real-transport in host file; each main independent.

# Known Follow-ups (Out of Scope)

1. Runtime must replace 14 stub builtins: unix_bind/accept/connect/read/write/close (6), tcp_bind/accept/connect/read/write/close (6), runtime_spawn/cancel/sleep_ms/spawn_periodic (4). Plus 9 cap probe stubs. The .oo code is production.
2. G11 real-cap tests (G30): currently report "skip" because the runtime probe stubs return -1. When the runtime replaces them, the cert line flips to "pass".
3. G27 push heartbeat, G28 concurrent accept, G29 wall-clock compact: each returns invalid handle when the runtime lacks the G26 scheduler.
4. G21T wall-clock and G21S concurrent require runtime thread support.
5. G24 test growth: prefer new files over expanding test_t4_mcp_protocol.oo past 200 lines.
